{"unit":6,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 6","tracks":{"a65":"Track_6.5.mp3"},"SEGS":{"interview":["a65",4.06,142.62]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 6 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Machines and weather</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 6, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;5. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u6\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">The car slows down on its own when the gap ahead closes &mdash; it&hellip; automatically.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">overtakes</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">brakes</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">commutes</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">There has been no rain here for eleven months. The region is in a serious&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">landslide</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">heatwave</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">drought</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">The lorry pulled out and&hellip; three cars in one go.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">overtook</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">injured</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">parked</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">Nothing was hurt except the door. Everything else was&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">unemployable</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">replaceable</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">helpless</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match the two halves of each phrase. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"m1\">a speed</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"m2\">a driving</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"m3\">a weather</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"m4\">climate</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"m5\">in</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"m3\" data-short=\"pattern\">pattern</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"m5\" data-short=\"control\">control</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"m1\" data-short=\"limit\">limit</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"m4\" data-short=\"change\">change</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"m2\" data-short=\"test\">test</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with one word from the box: <b>increase &middot; prevent &middot; explore</b>.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">There has been a sharp <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"increase\" data-why=\"An <b>increase</b> in something &mdash; the noun.\"> in the number of landslides.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">Nothing can <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"prevent\" data-why=\"<b>Prevent</b> something from happening.\"> a storm, only warn people about it.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">Scientists have been trying to <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"explore\" data-why=\"<b>Explore</b> an idea = examine it carefully.\"> the idea for years.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct relative word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">The engineer&hellip; built it works for a small company in Almaty.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">which</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">who</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">whose</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">My car,&hellip; I bought in 2019, has done ninety thousand kilometres.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">that</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">who</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">which</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">That is the junction&hellip; the accident happened.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">where</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">which</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">that</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">They interviewed the driver&hellip; licence had been taken away.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">who</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">which</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">whose</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Can you leave the relative word out? Choose.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">The device <b>that</b> I ordered has arrived. <select data-answer=\"Y\" data-why=\"<i>yes, it can go</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">no, it must stay</option><option value=\"Y\">yes, it can go</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">The car <b>that</b> drives itself is already on the roads. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"<i>no, it must stay</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">no, it must stay</option><option value=\"Y\">yes, it can go</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">My phone, <b>which</b> I bought in May, is already broken. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"In a non-defining clause the relative word can never be dropped.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"Y\">yes, it can go</option><option value=\"N\">no, it must stay</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>rain</i>) It <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"has been raining\" data-why=\"<i>How long</i>, still going on &rarr; present perfect continuous.\"> since Tuesday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>publish</i>) Meteorologists <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"have published\" data-why=\"A countable, finished result &rarr; present perfect simple.\"> eleven papers on it so far.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>always / know</i>) We <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"have always known\" data-why=\"<i>Know</i> is a state verb &mdash; never continuous.\"> that the climate moves.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">The drone, <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"which\" data-why=\"After a comma only <b>which</b> is possible, never <i>that</i>.\"> cost a fortune, was lost on the first flight.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">How much rainfall <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"has fallen\" data-why=\"<i>How much</i> asks for the finished total &rarr; present perfect simple: <i>has fallen</i>.\"> since 2010?</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">The correspondent reported the drought. She works for the BBC.<br>The correspondent <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"who reported the drought works for the bbc|who works for the bbc reported the drought\" data-why=\"A person, defining &rarr; <b>who</b>.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">Temperatures started rising ten years ago and they are still rising.<br>Temperatures <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"have been rising for ten years|'ve been rising for ten years\" data-why=\"An unfinished activity over a period &rarr; present perfect continuous + <b>for</b>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The machine that cannot say why</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">A system which reads medical scans better than most doctors is now in use in several countries. Nobody, including the people who built it, can explain how it decides.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>In 2018 a hospital group in the north of England began testing software which had been trained on two million chest scans. Within a year it was finding early signs of disease that experienced radiologists had missed, and missing almost nothing they had found. The doctors who ran the trial, most of whom had been sceptical at the start, described the results as uncomfortable rather than exciting.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>The discomfort has a name. A system of this kind does not follow rules that a person wrote down; it has been building its own, silently, out of the examples it was given. When a radiologist marks a scan, she can say which shadow made her decide. When the software does it, there is no sentence to produce. It is right, and it cannot say why.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>That matters more in medicine than almost anywhere else, because a doctor who cannot explain a decision cannot be argued with, and a patient who cannot argue has lost something. Several hospitals have therefore settled on a rule which sounds modest and is not: the machine may look first, but a human being signs. Nobody is allowed to act on the software alone.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>The engineers, whose work is often described as finished when the system passes its tests, say the interesting problem is only beginning. They have been developing tools which try to show which part of an image the software was attending to. The pictures those tools produce are suggestive rather than conclusive. Meanwhile the scans keep arriving, and the machine keeps being right, and the argument about whether that is enough has barely started.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">The doctors described the results as &ldquo;uncomfortable&rdquo; because\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the software made a large number of mistakes</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">they had been forced to use it</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">it was right without being able to explain itself</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">What rule have several hospitals agreed on?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the software may look first, but a person must sign</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the software may only be used at night</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the software must be switched off if a doctor disagrees</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">The software was trained on two million scans. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A says so directly.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">Most of the doctors in the trial expected it to work. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph A: most of them <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">The software is cheaper than employing radiologists. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"Cost is never mentioned anywhere in the text.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The tools that show what the software attended to give a complete explanation. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph D: they are <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, why does the writer say the rule &ldquo;sounds modest and is not&rdquo;?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">because it is very expensive to follow</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">because a small-sounding rule decides who is responsible</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">because most hospitals ignore it</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">The last sentence suggests that the writer thinks the debate is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">finished, and the machines have won</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">unnecessary, because the software works</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">only just beginning, while the technology moves ahead</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('interview',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> The World Today &middot; the interview\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 6.5</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the notes with one word.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">Cloud seeding does not solve a drought, because in a drought there are probably no <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"clouds\" data-why=\"No <b>clouds</b> in the sky to seed.\"> to seed.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">The scientists in Geneva are using <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"lasers\" data-why=\"They use <b>lasers</b> instead of chemicals.\"> instead of chemicals.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">They think the same technology could direct <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"lightning\" data-why=\"Directing <b>lightning</b> away from certain buildings.\"> away from certain buildings.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">When the presenter says &ldquo;That can&rsquo;t be a good idea, can it?&rdquo;, he is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">worried</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">enthusiastic</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">completely neutral</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Neil says we have been changing the weather for a long time anyway in order to\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">apologize for the research</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">change the subject</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">argue that the new technology is small compared with what we already do</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">The one worry Neil accepts about creating rain is that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the lasers are very noisy</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">rain made in one place may be taken from another</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the rain would be too heavy</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You have to move a meeting with a client, and you want to open the bad news.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Thursday any good?</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Unfortunately there has been a change of plan.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">I look forward to hearing from you.</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You are proposing a new time, and leaving the choice open.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Move it to Thursday.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">I am afraid I cannot move it.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Would it be possible to reschedule for Thursday afternoon?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You want to show the reader you have already sorted out part of the problem.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">I have already spoken to Marat, who has confirmed that either time is fine.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Apologies for any inconvenience.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Something has come up.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each line belong?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">Apologies for any inconvenience.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Phone\">How about getting together after work instead?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">Would it be possible to reschedule for later the same day?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Phone\">Let me just have a look at my diary&hellip;</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Mail\"><h5>The written email</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Phone\"><h5>The phone call</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the email in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"c2,c4,c1,c3\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"c1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Would it be possible to reschedule for later the same day? I am free from two o&rsquo;clock.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"c2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I am writing about our meeting on Thursday at eleven.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"c3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Apologies for any inconvenience. Kind regards, Aigerim</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"c4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Unfortunately there has been a change of plan: I have been asked to attend a client presentation.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Yerlan</b>Did you get to the site in the end?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>No. The junction <select data-answer=\"where\" data-why=\"A place &rarr; <b>where</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>which</option><option>that</option><option>where</option></select> the roadworks are was closed all morning.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Yerlan</b>Again? They have been at it for months.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Since March. They <select data-answer=\"have been resurfacing\" data-why=\"An unfinished activity over a period &rarr; present perfect continuous.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>have been resurfacing</option><option>have resurfaced</option><option>are resurfacing</option></select> the same two hundred metres.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Yerlan</b>How much have they actually finished?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>They <select data-answer=\"have laid\" data-why=\"<i>have laid</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>have been laying</option><option>have laid</option><option>are laying</option></select> about half of it. My car, <select data-answer=\"which\" data-why=\"After a comma, only <b>which</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>that</option><option>which</option><option>who</option></select> I only bought in spring, is covered in dust.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Yerlan</b>So what about the meeting?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"Would it be possible to\" data-why=\"An indirect proposal for a new time.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Would it be possible to</option><option>You need to</option><option>I want you to</option></select> move it to Friday? <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> <select data-answer=\"If the road opens,\" data-why=\"A real possibility &rarr; present simple after <i>If the road opens,</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>If the road will open,</option><option>If the road opened,</option><option>If the road opens,</option></select> I can be there by nine.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 100&ndash;120 words. Give yourself twenty minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> You cannot attend a meeting you agreed to two weeks ago. Write a professional email. Name the meeting first, give the change and the reason together, offer two possible new times without being asked, say what you have already sorted out, and close with one apology.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"Dear&hellip;   I am writing about&hellip;   Unfortunately there has been a change of plan:&hellip;   Would it be possible to&hellip;   I have already&hellip;   Apologies for any inconvenience.\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your email must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>the meeting named in the <b>first</b> sentence</li>\n        <li>one <b>non-defining relative clause</b> with a comma and <i>which</i> or <i>who</i></li>\n        <li>one <b>present perfect</b> for what you have already sorted out</li>\n        <li><b>Would it be possible to&hellip;?</b> and a second option offered</li>\n        <li>one apology, once &mdash; not three times</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; define it, then argue it</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Describe three machines or services you use, defining each one without naming it &mdash; <i>it is a device that&hellip;, it is a place where&hellip;</i> <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>should a machine be allowed to make a decision it cannot explain?</i> Give your view and one reason.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>three different relative words: <b>that / which, who, where</b> or <b>whose</b></li>\n        <li>one present perfect continuous for something still going on</li>\n        <li>one present perfect simple for a finished result</li>\n        <li>never <i>that</i> after a comma</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>It&rsquo;s a device that&hellip; &middot; It&rsquo;s a place where&hellip; &middot; It&rsquo;s somebody whose job is&hellip; &middot; They&rsquo;ve been &hellip;ing since&hellip; &middot; They&rsquo;ve already&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my email names the meeting before it says anything else</li>\n        <li>the change and the reason are in one sentence, not two paragraphs</li>\n        <li>I offered a second time without being asked</li>\n        <li>I said what I had already sorted out</li>\n        <li>I apologized once, and only once</li>\n        <li>I used three different relative words when I spoke</li>\n        <li>I never used <i>that</i> after a comma</li>\n        <li>I used the continuous for what is still going on and the simple for what is finished</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}